1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,144
Aziz is in a lift, between the fourth and the fifth floor, when his phone loses the network.

2
00:00:06,194 --> 00:00:09,552
One second earlier, MyID finished the check of his face.

3
00:00:09,602 --> 00:00:12,432
So did the check pass, or did it vanish?

4
00:00:12,482 --> 00:00:21,168
In Lesson 14, Aziz accepted the consent screen, and the platform wrote an acceptance record that permits one session at MyID.

5
00:00:21,218 --> 00:00:30,120
This lesson follows that one session: who opens it, what travels back to the platform, and what happens when something goes wrong on the way.

6
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:33,024
Start one step earlier, in the marketplace app.

7
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:37,992
Aziz wants to pay for a laptop in instalments, and the instalments need level two.

8
00:00:38,042 --> 00:00:41,088
The marketplace asks the platform for a step-up.

9
00:00:41,138 --> 00:00:47,904
The platform never refuses a step-up, but its answer to a side app is an instruction: continue in the mobile bank.

10
00:00:47,954 --> 00:00:53,688
If the marketplace still asks for a proofing session, it gets an error, and no session opens.

11
00:00:53,738 --> 00:00:55,560
Why this rule?

12
00:00:55,610 --> 00:01:03,192
The mobile bank is the master app: it moves money, and the bank's team adds the MyID package to it, and to no other app.

13
00:01:03,242 --> 00:01:09,168
Only one app holds the camera that checks faces against state records, so only one app must be defended.

14
00:01:09,218 --> 00:01:15,744
I think this is the right trade: one more tap for Aziz, and one door for an attacker instead of one in every app.

15
00:01:15,794 --> 00:01:20,016
So Aziz opens the mobile bank, and accepts the consent there.

16
00:01:20,066 --> 00:01:23,400
Now the backend opens the session, not the app.

17
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:28,512
The platform calls MyID with the credentials of the installation, which never go to the phone.

18
00:01:28,562 --> 00:01:34,080
It sends the threshold of the bank: the minimum face match that MyID must apply.

19
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:39,528
It gets back a session identifier, and gives a handle to the mobile bank on this same device.

20
00:01:39,578 --> 00:01:42,696
This is the proofing session, and it is now Open.

21
00:01:42,746 --> 00:01:49,128
It belongs to one customer, one device and one purpose, here a step-up, so it is a full proofing.

22
00:01:49,178 --> 00:01:52,824
It lives for ten minutes, a value that MyID sets.

23
00:01:52,874 --> 00:01:56,520
While it is open, no second session can open for Aziz.

24
00:01:56,570 --> 00:02:01,800
Inside the mobile bank, the MyID screen captures his document and his face.

25
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:07,416
MyID checks that the face is live, and compares the face and the document with the state records.

26
00:02:07,466 --> 00:02:11,184
Then it gives the app one thing: a one-time result code.

27
00:02:11,234 --> 00:02:13,608
The result code is not the result.

28
00:02:13,658 --> 00:02:18,432
It is a ticket that only the platform can exchange, within five minutes, one time.

29
00:02:18,482 --> 00:02:22,200
The app sends the code and the session identifier to the platform.

30
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:29,616
The platform accepts the code only from the device and the customer of the session, only while the session is Open, and only once.

31
00:02:29,666 --> 00:02:33,360
Then it calls MyID, exchanges the code, and gets the result.

32
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:36,408
Now imagine that the code was copied on the way.

33
00:02:36,458 --> 00:02:38,904
Someone sends it again, from a different phone.

34
00:02:38,954 --> 00:02:43,368
The platform refuses it: wrong device, or code already used.

35
00:02:43,418 --> 00:02:45,240
It writes a security event.

36
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:49,224
And it never stores the result code, so there is nothing to steal later.

37
00:02:49,274 --> 00:02:53,328
On success, the platform checks every field before it keeps it.

38
00:02:53,378 --> 00:02:57,168
The personal identification number must have fourteen digits.

39
00:02:57,218 --> 00:03:03,384
A document with an expiry date in the past is a failure, even when MyID says success.

40
00:03:03,434 --> 00:03:08,352
A face match below the bank's own minimum is a failure too: face not matched.

41
00:03:08,402 --> 00:03:12,744
Then the verified identity is kept, and the session is Succeeded.

42
00:03:12,794 --> 00:03:22,968
Aziz sees his names, his date of birth, the last four characters of his document number, and the first two and last two digits of his personal identification number, and he confirms them.

43
00:03:23,018 --> 00:03:24,864
Failures get plain words.

44
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:28,800
On Aziz's first try, a lamp makes a glare on his document.

45
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:37,440
MyID gives a reason code, the platform turns it into a reason key, poor image, and Aziz reads: try again now, without the glare.

46
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:39,864
He never sees a code or a provider name.

47
00:03:39,914 --> 00:03:45,384
A failure that the person or the capture caused is counted against the limits of Lesson 11.

48
00:03:45,434 --> 00:03:48,648
A failure that the service caused is not counted.

49
00:03:48,698 --> 00:03:56,736
When MyID is down, Aziz reads that the service is temporarily not available, his level does not move, and he can try again later.

50
00:03:56,786 --> 00:03:58,512
There is no deferred proofing.

51
00:03:58,562 --> 00:04:00,384
And the lift?

52
00:04:00,434 --> 00:04:06,408
When the network comes back, the app reports that the check is complete, but no code reached the platform.

53
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:12,840
The platform waits until MyID closes the session, and then asks MyID for the session status.

54
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:17,664
A code is there, so the exchange continues, and the check did not vanish.

55
00:04:17,714 --> 00:04:23,136
If no code had been there, the attempt would not count, and Aziz could simply try again.

56
00:04:23,186 --> 00:04:36,336
To recap: only the master app runs MyID, the platform opens the session with credentials that stay in the bank, the app carries back a one-use code, and every failure has a key, a counting rule and plain words.

57
00:04:36,386 --> 00:04:38,736
Aziz is now at level two.

58
00:04:38,786 --> 00:04:40,488
Next year, he buys a new phone.

59
00:04:40,538 --> 00:04:43,080
Must he show his passport to MyID again?

60
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:44,952
Next: prove once.
